---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import EmailCta from '../components/EmailCta.astro';
import VideoGallery from '../components/VideoGallery.astro';
import { urls } from '../data/urls';
import { aboutVideos } from '../data/videos';
import PhotoGallery from '../components/PhotoGallery.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { lib, photo } from '../data/library';
import { founders, founderUrl } from '../data/founders';

const currentTeam = founders.filter((f) => f.active);
const otherFounders = founders.filter((f) => !f.active);

const impact = [
	{ value: '1000+', label: 'teachers taught to code' },
	{ value: '12,000+', label: 'kids introduced to STEM education' },
	{ value: '30,000+', label: 'books sold in Australia' },
	{ value: '46', label: 'official company teapots' },
];

const pipeline = [
	{ age: 'By age 6', fact: 'Children classify jobs as male and female.' },
	{ age: 'By age 8', fact: 'They are limiting aspirations.' },
	{ age: 'By 13', fact: 'They rule out careers that don’t fit gender stereotypes.' },
	{ age: 'By 16–17', fact: 'Around 60% of girls aspire to stereotypically “female” jobs.' },
];
---

<Layout
	title="About Us — Girl Geek Academy"
	description="Girls who love tech still get pushed out of it. Meet the founders of Girl Geek Academy, and find out how we accidentally ran the world’s first all-women hackathon."
>
	<Header />
	<main>
		<section class="about-hero section">
			<div class="container grid-2">
				<div>
				<p class="about-hero__eyebrow">About us</p>
				<h1>Get ya geek on!</h1>
				<p class="about-hero__lead">
					<strong>Girls who love tech still get pushed out of it. We keep them in.</strong>
				</p>
				<p>
					Our CEO Sarah Moran learned to code at five and was pushed out of tech in Year 10. Girl Geek
					Academy exists so the next generation of girl geeks stay.
				</p>
				<p>
					Women and girls shape the technology that shapes their lives. We ran the world’s first
					all-women hackathon in 2014. Then we realised: if we’d started teaching children 10 years
					ago, we could be hiring them today.
				</p>
				<p>
					So now our programs teach women, girls and families across games, startups, 3D printing,
					design, software, hardware, AI, space, aviation and robotics — and we partner with teachers,
					parents, corporates and governments to keep girl geeks in.
				</p>
				<div class="about-hero__ctas">
					<a href={urls.workWithUs} class="btn btn-primary">Work with Us</a>
					<a href={urls.techInSchools} class="btn btn-coral">Policy &amp; Impact</a>
				</div>
				</div>
				<div class="hero-media hero-media--wide">
					<Image src={lib('photos/49481000838_554803bda8_c.jpg')} alt="The Girl Geek Academy crew holding a big pink Girl Geek Academy banner" width={800} />
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="about-origin section section--dark">
			<div class="container">
				<p class="about-origin__eyebrow">Our girl gang · 2014</p>
				<h2>We accidentally ran the first all-women hackathon in the world</h2>
				<div class="grid-2 about-origin__grid">
					<div>
						<p>
							We were going to tech events, but they were usually held in dark basements where they
							fed us beer, pizza and energy drinks. (We like those things — but we have our limits.)
							Our mates were happy we came, but they’d ask: “Why don’t more girls come to our
							events?”
						</p>
						<p>
							So we designed a hackathon <em>we</em> wanted to go to — as an example of how great
							tech events can be. We had tea and cupcakes. And yoga. And sunlight! We ran the first
							#SheHacks for International Women’s Day 2014.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div>
						<p>
							We tried to find other women and non-binary folk running similar hackathons so we
							could be their friends. We looked and looked — and realised no one had run one before.
							We’d accidentally run the first all-women hackathon in the world.
						</p>
						<p>
							We thought: if no one has done this very basic thing to support us, who’s working on
							the hard stuff? That’s when we knew we had a responsibility to do so. In July 2014 we
							founded Girl Geek Academy as a company and a global movement — and we’ve been building
							a world where tech isn’t just a boy’s club ever since.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="about-pipeline section">
			<div class="container">
				<h2 class="text-center">Tech has a pipeline problem</h2>
				<p class="text-center about-pipeline__intro">Let’s talk about the holes in the pipe.</p>
				<Image
					src={lib('graphics/Artboard-1rainbow.png')}
					alt="A rainbow showing the pipeline: kids, teens, college, mid career, leadership"
					width={360}
					class="about-graphic"
				/>
				<div class="about-pipeline__grid">
					{
						pipeline.map((s) => (
							<div class="about-pipeline__card">
								<p class="about-pipeline__age">{s.age}</p>
								<p>{s.fact}</p>
							</div>
						))
					}
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="about-impact section section--dark">
			<div class="container">
				<h2 class="text-center">Gender inequality ain’t gonna fix itself</h2>
				<p class="text-center about-impact__intro">
					Since we launched, we’ve achieved more than we could have imagined — including:
				</p>
				<div class="about-impact__stats">
					{
						impact.map((n) => (
							<div class="about-impact__stat">
								<span class="about-impact__value">{n.value}</span>
								<span class="about-impact__label">{n.label}</span>
							</div>
						))
					}
				</div>
				<div class="about-impact__graphics">
					<Image src={lib('graphics/Artboard-3teapot.png')} alt="A teapot with a pixel heart — one of our 46 official company teapots" width={260} />
					<Image src={lib('graphics/Artboard-3world.png')} alt="Map of milestones: Girl Geek Academy founded in Australia 2014, SheHacks NYC 2017, Ukraine book launch 2020, Girl Geek Samoa launched January 2020" width={520} />
				</div>
				<p class="text-center about-impact__more">
					Through grants, tenders, corporate clients and fundraising, we’ve prototyped what works —
					and campaigned in media for change.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section id="team" class="about-founders section">
			<div class="container">
				<Image
					src={lib('graphics/Artboard-4girl-gang.png')}
					alt="Illustration of three girl geeks gathered around a laptop"
					width={300}
					class="about-graphic"
				/>
				<h2 class="text-center">Meet our founders</h2>
				<p class="text-center about-founders__intro">
					Five of us started Girl Geek Academy in 2014. Four of us run it today.
				</p>
				<Image
					src={lib('photos/GGA_group_1.jpg')}
					alt="A selfie of the five Girl Geek Academy founders"
					width={900}
					class="about-founders__photo"
				/>
				<h3 class="text-center about-founders__group">Running Girl Geek Academy today</h3>
				<ul class="about-founders__list">
					{
						currentTeam.map((f) => (
							<li class="about-founders__card">
								<p class="about-founders__name">{f.name}</p>
								<p class="about-founders__role">{f.role}</p>
																<p class="about-founders__bio">{f.summary}</p>
								{f.hasPage !== false && (
									<a href={founderUrl(f)} class="about-founders__more">Read {f.name.split(' ')[0]}’s story →</a>
								)}
							</li>
						))
					}
				</ul>
				<h3 class="text-center about-founders__group">Also a co-founder</h3>
				<ul class="about-founders__list">
					{
						otherFounders.map((f) => (
							<li class="about-founders__card">
								<p class="about-founders__name">{f.name}</p>
								<p class="about-founders__role">{f.role}</p>
																<p class="about-founders__bio">{f.summary}</p>
								{f.hasPage !== false && (
									<a href={founderUrl(f)} class="about-founders__more">Read {f.name.split(' ')[0]}’s story →</a>
								)}
							</li>
						))
					}
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<VideoGallery
			id="as-seen"
			heading="As seen on…"
			intro="TV and radio — including ABC Breakfast, ABC News, ABC Pacific (Beyond Awesome), Download This Show, The Project, Scope and The Today Show."
			videos={aboutVideos}
			dark
		/>

		<PhotoGallery
			heading="Our community"
			photos={[
				photo('photos/Girl-Geek-Academy-2017.jpg', 'The Girl Geek Academy team in 2017'),
				photo('photos/28977304673_f8bb9cafaa_b.jpeg', 'A big group of girl geeks with their hands in the air'),
				photo('photos/48862709223_31c22e90a4_k.jpg', 'A huge crowd cheering under colourful banners'),
				photo('photos/33212012648_79d284a124_k.jpg', 'A group photo in front of a Girl Geek Academy backdrop'),
				photo('photos/47087032121_4b8e8ace19_k.jpg', 'Three women laughing together at a laptop'),
				photo('photos/46173470245_45d92b28f7_k.jpg', 'Participants working at laptops in front of a mural'),
				photo('photos/48862705028_32cc3392ea_k.jpg', 'Two girl geeks smiling in front of a patterned wall'),
				photo('photos/40959447385_3182f15d57_c.jpg', 'Two girls smiling in front of a Girl Geek Academy backdrop'),
				photo('photos/47087031901_df9fa54346_k.jpg', 'Participants working together at a table'),
				photo('photos/48862896413_b014c41c4d_c.jpg', 'A facilitator helping participants at laptops'),
				photo('photos/28653703406_e9a4b5bb1d_c.jpg', 'Two women working at a laptop by a window'),
				photo('photos/033-1.jpg', 'Two women chatting at a laptop in front of a mural'),
				photo('photos/33212010908_2325093649_k.jpg', 'Three girls holding a #GirlGeekAcademy sign'),
				photo('photos/48863207446_3e485b2fc9_k.jpg', 'Participants chatting around a table'),
				photo('photos/48863440482_239545beaf_k.jpg', 'A panel in front of a tinsel backdrop'),
				photo('graphics/Artboard-1tall.png', 'Three young women laughing at a laptop'),
				photo('photos/LetterBoard.jpg', 'A #GirlGeekAcademy letter board with coffee cups'),
				photo('photos/GGA-Thumb-WhatIsGGA.jpg', 'A huge group of girl geeks sitting together on the floor'),
				photo('photos/26989912417_8cd1920558_c.jpg', 'Girls gathered around a laptop'),
				photo('photos/33212013388_4063420c2d_k-1.jpg', 'Women at laptops in a bright room'),
				photo('photos/043-1.jpg', 'Girls playing games at a row of computers'),
				photo('photos/050.jpg', 'Girls in headphones at a row of computers'),
				photo('graphics/Artboard-2PLE.png', 'Girls gaming together at computers'),
				photo('photos/48862726863_c140244ddf_k.jpg', 'Lanyards, badges and stickers laid out on a table'),
				photo('photos/26641465358_c782ea4d12_w.jpg', 'Two women chatting beside a table of gift bags'),
				photo('photos/40512120271_3bdcae56ff_w.jpg', 'Three women chatting at an event'),
				photo('photos/25795454347_6cd6caaf6c_w.jpg', 'A group of women at a formal event'),
				photo('photos/48863026926_9ec8422396_w.jpg', 'A participant raising her hand to ask a question'),
				photo('photos/28977327113_cec9d4d568_w.jpg', 'Four women laughing together at a laptop'),
			]}
		/>

		<section class="about-programs section">
			<div class="container text-center">
				<Image
					src={lib('graphics/Artboard-54Rainbow-light.png')}
					alt="Helping women build the internet — a rainbow and globe illustration"
					width={320}
					class="about-graphic"
				/>
				<h2>Get ya geek on with us</h2>
				<p>
					From MissMakesCode workshops to #SheHacks and beyond — explore our programs, or partner with
					us to bring them to your school, workplace or community.
				</p>
				<div class="about-programs__links">
					<a href={urls.missMakesCode} class="btn btn-yellow">MissMakesCode</a>
					<a href={urls.sheHacks} class="btn btn-coral">SheHacks</a>
					<a href={urls.workWithUs} class="btn btn-mint">Work with Us</a>
					<EmailCta label="Partner with us for 2027" variant="primary" />
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
	<Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
	.about-graphic {
		margin: 0 auto 2rem;
		height: auto;
	}

	.about-impact__graphics {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		justify-content: center;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 2rem;
		margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem;
	}

	.about-impact__graphics img {
		height: auto;
		max-width: 100%;
	}

	.about-founders__photo {
		width: 100%;
		max-width: 720px;
		height: auto;
		margin: 0 auto 2.5rem;
		border-radius: 0.25rem;
	}

	.about-hero {
		background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--color-yellow-light) 0%, var(--color-white) 100%);
	}

	.about-hero__eyebrow,
	.about-origin__eyebrow {
		font-family: var(--font-pinata);
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.06em;
		margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
	}

	.about-origin__eyebrow {
		color: var(--color-yellow);
	}

	.about-hero__lead {
		font-size: 1.25rem;
		max-width: 40rem;
	}

	.about-hero__ctas,
	.about-programs__links {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
	}

	.about-programs__links {
		justify-content: center;
	}

	.about-origin__grid {
		align-items: start;
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
	}

	.about-pipeline__intro,
	.about-impact__intro,
	.about-founders__intro {
		max-width: 36rem;
		margin: 0 auto 2rem;
	}

	.about-pipeline__grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
		gap: 1rem;
	}

	.about-pipeline__card {
		padding: 1.25rem;
		border: 1px solid rgba(95, 125, 215, 0.25);
		border-radius: 0.25rem;
	}

	.about-pipeline__age {
		font-family: var(--font-pinata);
		text-transform: uppercase;
		margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
		color: var(--color-coral);
	}

	.about-pipeline__card p:last-child {
		margin: 0;
	}

	.about-impact__stats {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
		gap: 1rem;
		text-align: center;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	.about-impact__value {
		display: block;
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
		line-height: 1;
		color: var(--color-yellow);
		margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
	}

	.about-impact__label {
		font-size: 0.95rem;
	}

	.about-impact__more {
		max-width: 40rem;
		margin: 0 auto;
	}

		.about-founders__list {
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
		padding: 0;
				display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		justify-content: center;
		gap: 1.5rem;
	}

	.about-founders__list > li {
		flex: 1 1 240px;
		max-width: 340px;
	}

	.about-founders__group {
		margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
	}

	.about-founders__more {
		display: inline-block;
		margin-top: 0.75rem;
		font-weight: 600;
	}

	.about-founders__card {
		padding: 1.5rem;
		border: 1px solid rgba(95, 125, 215, 0.2);
		border-radius: 0.25rem;
	}

	.about-founders__name {
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
		line-height: 1;
		margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
	}

	.about-founders__role {
		font-family: var(--font-pinata);
		text-transform: uppercase;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
		color: var(--color-coral);
	}

	.about-founders__bio {
		margin: 0;
	}

	@media (max-width: 991px) {
		.about-pipeline__grid,
		.about-impact__stats {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
		}
	}
</style>
